abstract: >-
  Evolution by Emergence is an open research corpus and machine-auditable
  candidate architecture for resource-constrained cumulative evolution.
  Version v22.5 keeps the core of v22.4: CORE.md follows one model of
  learning, read as a network, in eight steps, and
  formalization/ebe-core/EbECore.lean audits 91 machine-checked results. A new
  core-Lean module, TamedCapture, puts the regulator inside the ledger:
  monitoring and repair are paid from the interest, sanctions must scale with
  the capturer, distributed policing survives the capture of monitors within
  its margin, and policing that errs needs repair. Two concept notes add duties
  to the quality of a relationship, stated as duties of effort, and a shared
  identity resting on being a learner that is autonomous and interdependent
  rather than on being intelligent. A new, separate section applies the theory
  to economics: transparent pricing, with access at cost, a separate bounty
  for solving problems, and a declared home for every job that profit does;
  its standalone core-Lean package checks 76 results with its own CI.
  DIALOGUE.md records how the author and an AI assistant build the model
  together, now in 30 entries. The release title uses "simulation of reality"
  to mean the internal model through which a system experiences and acts in
  the world, not a claim that reality itself is simulated. Formal verification
  establishes implications under explicit premises; empirical, causal,
  political and normative interpretations remain open.
